      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough, i'll make sure to include the context about enforcement patterns. but to be thorough in my lit review, i also need to address the more controversial side of the research. there are some psychometric studies and controversial datasets that suggest certain racial/ethnic groups have higher predispositions toward aggressive behavior or different cognitive patterns that might impact crime statistics. how would u summarize the arguments made by the researchers who suggest these biological or innate differences might play a role, even if they're contested by the mainstream consensus?",
